 {"status": "pending", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-25", "title": "[P3] A same-id downgrade to warn loses the rule's block_message - the user is told `would have blocked: Command blocked by security policy.` instead of why", "priority": "P3", "cell": "interruptor warn mode", "detail": "With a same-id override (`action: warn`) in rules.d, the verdict the CLI prints is `terminal-jail: WARNING - would have blocked: Command blocked by security policy.` The generic placeholder replaces the rule's own block_message, so the warning does not say which policy was downgraded or what it protects - and warn mode exists precisely so an operator can decide whether the downgrade is safe. The engine does emit the right rule_id. Fix direction: carry the matched rule's block_message through the warn path instead of the generic string, and add a bridge test asserting the downgraded rule's message appears in `reason`.", "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-19 real-use run, same-id override verification", "created_at": "2026-09-19T10:08:54.469192+00:00", "source": "dogfood lane 2026-09-19 (docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md)", "attempts": 0}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-26", "title": "[P2] SKIPPED-install-bunker (2026-09-19): spawn cancelled fleet-wide at 30-45s while the server-side rootless-docker install needs 60-90s; cancellations leak users (17 on las-03, 46 on las-02)", "priority": "P2", "cell": "bunker install leg (INFRA - not this repo's foreman)", "detail": "`bunker spawn --server bunker-las-03` -> deadline_exceeded (3rd consecutive run) AND `--server bunker-las-02` -> deadline_exceeded (las-02 succeeded 2026-09-18). New root cause from `journalctl -u bunkerd`: on las-03 the rootless-docker install COMPLETED (dockerd 29.8.1 up, `docker version` returned server info, docker.service enabled) but the spawn was cancelled at 45.4s and discarded (`signal: killed`, context canceled); on las-02 it was cancelled at 29.9s at `enable linger`. In both cases the rollback `userdel` also failed with `context canceled`, so every cancelled spawn leaks its user - 17 bunker-* users on las-03, 46 on las-02 (my two half-spawns bunker-659255d5 and bunker-83f632fc were cleaned: userdel -r + /home + /run/user removed). las-02 also logs `no host SSH public key found, agent will not accept host connections`. The client deadline is shorter than the work it cancels, and the client cancel destroys in-flight server work. Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md section 6. Install leg was stood in by a documented install on las-02 as a plain account in a scratch HOME. Owner: infra, not this repo's foreman.", "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-19 install leg attempt + bunkerd log forensics", "created_at": "2026-09-19T10:08:54.469192+00:00", "source": "dogfood lane 2026-09-19 (docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md)", "attempts": 0}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-27", "title": "[P1] A live bunkerd token has been sitting world-readable in /tmp since 2026-09-15, left by a dogfood run's scratch HOME", "priority": "P1", "cell": "dogfood/infra hygiene (INFRA - not this repo's foreman)", "detail": "`/tmp/dogfood-tj/home/.bunker/config.yaml` (mode 644, owner kara, mtime 2026-09-15 05:10) contains `name: bunker-las-03` plus a token line. Its sha256 matches the token in `/etc/bunkerd/config.yaml` on the live host - it is the CURRENT token, not a stale one. It was left behind by a previous dogfood run that redirected HOME into the scratch dir; /tmp/dogfood-tj is also world-traversable and holds that run's leftover secret.txt and scripts. No value is reproduced anywhere in this row, the integration report, or the dogfood log. Fix direction: (a) dogfood scratch HOMEs must never receive credential files - redirect $HOME to a 0700 dir and/or destroy the scratch tree at the end of every tick; (b) purge this file and rotate the bunkerd token (the token is live, so purge alone is not enough); (c) add a routine check for credential-shaped files under /tmp/dogfood-* to the dogfood tick. Owner: infra/dogfood protocol, not this repo's foreman.", "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-19 run, scratch-dir hygiene inspection", "created_at": "2026-09-19T10:08:54.469192+00:00", "source": "dogfood lane 2026-09-19 (docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md)", "attempts": 0}
